### What is a URL shortener?

A URL shortener maps a long URL to a short unique key, stores that mapping durably, and redirects any request for the short key back to the original URL. It is one of the most commonly asked system design interview questions because it touches key-value storage, caching, encoding, and scale.

### How do you generate the short key?

The cleanest approach is to assign each new URL a unique numeric id from a counter or database sequence, then base62-encode that number. Seven base62 characters cover over 3.5 trillion values.

```java
package com.bank.urlshortener;

public class Base62Encoder {
    private static final String ALPHABET =
        "0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ";

    public String encode(long id) {
        if (id == 0) return "0";
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        while (id > 0) {
            sb.append(ALPHABET.charAt((int) (id % 62)));
            id /= 62;
        }
        return sb.reverse().toString();
    }
}
```

### Why is caching critical?

A link is created once but clicked thousands of times, making the system extremely read-heavy. A cache like Redis in front of the database serves redirects in single-digit milliseconds.

```java
package com.bank.urlshortener;

public class UrlResolver {
    public String resolve(String shortKey) {
        String url = cache.get(shortKey);          // Redis GET
        if (url == null) {
            url = repository.findByKey(shortKey);  // DB lookup
            if (url != null) cache.put(shortKey, url); // populate cache
        }
        return url;
    }
}
```

### How do you handle custom aliases?

A user requests a specific key like "nbi-salary" and you must check it is not already taken. Use a unique constraint in the database; if the insert fails, the alias is taken.

### How do you handle expiration?

Store a TTL with the mapping. On resolve, check if the link has expired. A background job periodically cleans up expired entries.

### How do you track analytics?

Record each click asynchronously via a message queue so counting never slows the redirect. A consumer aggregates click counts per link.

```java
package com.bank.urlshortener;

public class ClickTracker {
    public void trackClick(String shortKey) {
        analyticsQueue.send(new ClickEvent(shortKey, Instant.now()));
        // Consumer aggregates counts; redirect is not slowed
    }
}
```

### What is the data model?

A simple mapping from short key to long URL, plus metadata: creation time, expiry, owner, and click counter.

```java
package com.bank.urlshortener;

public record UrlMapping(
    String shortKey,
    String longUrl,
    String owner,
    Instant createdAt,
    Instant expiresAt,
    long clickCount
) {}
```

### What about consistency?

A brand-new link might not be in every cache immediately, but eventual consistency on a redirect is acceptable because, unlike money, a short link appearing a second late harms nobody.

### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer knows to handle the rare collision case when using hash-based key generation, considers distributed id generation (Snowflake) for multi-region, and monitors cache hit ratios to ensure the cache is effective.
